    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51073" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgultum</span></b> , i, n.
		contr. from virguletum, from virgula (only in
		plur.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a bush</i>, <i>thicket</i>, <i>copse</i>, <i>shrubbery</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				3, 18 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 73</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Div. 1, 24, 49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Cael. 18, 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 14,
				7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. E. 10, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 5,
				661</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14, 349</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 2, 18,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 2,
			90</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Slips</i>, <i>cuttings</i> of trees: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">defodere in terram virgulta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 933</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silvestria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. G.
					2, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 346</span></i>.</div>
